# Keep it simple

- Prefer the simplest option that works for this small challenge app.
- No extreme abstraction, indirection, or “enterprise” patterns unless clearly needed.
- Names should be short, descriptive, and obvious (e.g. `chat-feed`, not `chat-layout__feed`).
- Flat CSS class names — do not use BEM `__` / `--` unless the user asks.
- Avoid premature generalization (extra wrappers, factories, context for one consumer).
- When two approaches work, choose the clearer one for a reviewer reading the PR in order.
